[[File:E 284.png|thumb|[[Zoge|Zoge]], the first example of a Zombie enemy]]
'''Zombie Enemies''' (Japanese: ゾンビ ''Zonbi'') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] introduced in [[Zombie Outbreaks]] and [[Legend Stages]]. Their designs are generally purple, sometimes with white accents. Most are characterized as having above-average stats, short range, low money drops, and two unique abilities: they can [[Burrow]] under your front lines to reach your cats behind the lines or even the [[Cat Base]], and they can [[Revive]] after being dead for a specific amount of time. The specifics of these abilities vary per enemy.

[[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer Cats]] prevent any Zombies they land the finishing blow on from reviving, while [[:Category:Soulstrike Cats|Soulstrike Cats]] can target and damage the remains left behind by Zombies between revives. The [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast Cannon]] has both of these properties in addition to freezing Zombies, dealing a % of their maximum health as damage and forcing all underground Zombies to the surface.

See [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Zombie abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Zombie enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Anti-Zombie abilities are improved by the [[Antimatter Fruit]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]].
*Zombie [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Zombie|Necro Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Zombie|Necro Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Zombie|Necro Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Rotten Dawn]], [[Rotten Apex]], [[Rotten Refuge]]
**[[Big Peng Z Strikes]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

