==Trivia==
*In Japan, white and purple are the two colors most commonly associated with death. Additionally, the kanji for purple (紫) and the kanji for death (死) both have the ''[[wikipedia:Kanji#On'yomi (Sino-Japanese reading)|on]]'' reading ''shi''.
*The only time a proper Zombie cat has been shown was in the thumbnail for the [https://youtu.be/NhKsytW96IE third episode] of [[Battle Cats TV]], which showed Prof. Cat as a Zombie, coinciding with [[Version 8.2 Update|Version 8.2]] and the addition of the "jump to [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]] stage" feature.
**[[The Burgle Cats/Roster|Walker]] from [[The Burgle Cats]] also looks Zombie-like, but isn't quite the same shade of purple.
*Although Purple [[Catfruit]] is often required for various True Form evolutions on anti-Zombie units and are similar in color to the Zombies themselves, they predate the introduction of Zombies, being initially associated with [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]]. This was not retroactively corrected, hence explaining their absence from [[Growing Purple]], which is still populated by Dark enemies.
*[[The Thrillerz]] are the only Zombie enemy to have a burrow limit of 2.
*[[Johnnyleon]] and [[Bears Be Back]] are the only Zombie enemies to lack the Revive ability.
**Despite their inability to revive, the [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] sound and graphic will play if they are defeated by a cat with that ability.
*[[Miss Haka]] and [[Big Sal]] are the only Zombie enemies that are able to [[Burrow]] an infinite amount of times.

